Written during a Master's research internship (M1 AIRE, Université Paris Cité)
on a study of open-ended survey responses from a challenge-based learning
programme, and released so that the methods can be inspected and reused.

The study was carried out within the ANR project Open Futures (OPEN-FUTURES),
"Open science and the future researcher: multi-level analysis of the iGEM
community-based open science ecosystem".

No survey data, participant text, or identifiers are included in this
repository. The corpus in broadlisten/sample.py is entirely synthetic and was
written to exercise the code; it is not an extract of any real dataset.

This software calls, but does not redistribute, the following models. Each is
downloaded at run time from its own source and carries its own licence, which
you are responsible for reading before use:

  Qwen3-Embedding (Alibaba Cloud)     https://huggingface.co/Qwen
  Qwen2.5-Instruct (Alibaba Cloud)    https://huggingface.co/Qwen
  BGE-M3 (BAAI)                       https://huggingface.co/BAAI/bge-m3
  en_core_web_sm (spaCy, MIT)         https://spacy.io/models/en

Methods implemented here follow published work, cited in the docstring of the
function that implements each one. The citations are attribution, not a claim
of endorsement by those authors.
